  "content": {
    "rendered": "<p>With summer coming up fast are you concerned about summer vacation parenting time?</p>\n<p>Hi, I’m Marie Drake of the Drake law firm. And I’m here to talk to you about summer and other holiday parenting time in Colorado. It’s always better to have a parenting time schedule that you to your spouse or ex-spouse and you have created together. And the reason is, is because it’s just going to be easier to follow something that you put together versus what a court orders you to do. The court doesn’t know your family and doesn’t know your children and doesn’t know you. So it’s better to compromise a little than have to go to a hearing and be ordered to follow something that you don’t think is fair. We know the holidays and summer vacation time can sometimes be stressful particularly trying to plan it. So here at the Drake law firm, we’re happy to help you put together an agreement that both sides can live with, and that is in the best interest of your children. So give us a call. We’re here to help.</p>\n<div class=\"ast-oembed-container \" style=\"height: 100%;\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Are You Concerned About Summer Vacation &amp; Your Shared Parenting Time?\" width=\"500\" height=\"375\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/8Y98R1wO5mU?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>\n"
  },
